 762:     def infer_dismissed_batters(self):
 763:         """DISABLED (Bug #2 fix).
 764: 
 765:         Previously this method tried to infer dismissals from the squad
 766:         XI order (e.g. "openers always bat", "players between this
 767:         position and the active position must have been dismissed").
 768:         That heuristic is fundamentally broken for T20 cricket because
 769:         teams routinely send non-openers up the order (e.g. KKR sent
 770:         Rahane to open instead of Narine in this match) and promote
 771:         nightwatchmen / Impact-Subs out of squad order.
 772: 
 773:         A player is now dismissed ONLY when there is direct evidence:
 774:           1. They were on the strip and then disappeared (replaced by
 775:              a new batter at the crease).
 776:           2. The wickets count increased at the same time.
 777:           3. Scout's action text describes a dismissal.
 778: 
 779:         Squad position is metadata for commentary context only — never
 780:         a state-change trigger. Wicket count is tracked separately in
 781:         `self._inn['wickets']` so disabling this does not affect the
 782:         score; it only stops phantom dismissals from corrupting the
 783:         batting card and seeding bad scorer hints.
 784:         """
 785:         # No-op preserved so existing call sites remain valid.
 786:         self._dismissed_inferred = True
 787:         return
