3218:     def _is_witnessed_dismissal(self, name: str) -> bool:
3219:         """True if `name` has a witnessed (non-placeholder) FOW entry.
3220: 
3221:         Canonical "is this batter a confirmed dismissal" check used by
3222:         invariant guards.  A name is a confirmed dismissal iff there is
3223:         a `fall_of_wickets` entry whose `batter == name`, with
3224:         `_witnessed=True` and not `_unwitnessed=True` (back-fill
3225:         placeholders carry `_unwitnessed=True`; real wicket events
3226:         stamp `_witnessed=True` via `_add_fow`, line ~2375).
3227: 
3228:         Used by:
3229:           * `update_batter()` un-dismiss prevention (refuses to un-
3230:             dismiss a batter the FOW says was actually out);
3231:           * `validate_state_consistency()` post-hoc resurrection demote
3232:             and FOW-preferred max-2 deactivation.
