 951: def _balls_to_overs_str(balls: int) -> str:
 952:     """Inverse of overs_to_balls. 6 -> '1.0', 11 -> '1.5', 13 -> '2.1'.
 953: 
 954:     Display-convention note: the 6th legal ball of an over is rendered
 955:     as the *next* over's `.0` position because of integer-divide
 956:     arithmetic — 71 balls -> '11.5' (5 legal balls into over 12) and
 957:     72 balls -> '12.0' (12 complete overs, 0 balls into over 13).
 958:     There is no '11.6' representation in this scheme; CB displays the
 959:     same ball as '11.6' (1-6 within-over), while the pipeline collapses
 960:     it into '12.0' (0-5 within-over plus a "completed" marker).  When
 961:     reconciling with CB ball-by-ball, treat pipeline `(N+1).0` as
 962:     equivalent to CB `(N).6`: a sequence like
 963:     `47/4 (11.5) → 51/4 (12.0)` represents the boundary on the 6th
 964:     ball of over 12 finishing the over with score 51/4.  Score and
 965:     over-count are correct; only the ball-position label differs.
 966:     """
 967:     return f"{balls // 6}.{balls % 6}"
